WEBVTT

00:09.570 --> 00:11.740
You dodged that attack?

00:12.200 --> 00:14.700
It seems it wasn't the multi-legged tank's abilities

00:14.700 --> 00:17.080
that overpowered an entire unit of the Imperial Army.

00:18.000 --> 00:20.790
And you seem too refined to be Alliance or Holy Republic.

00:21.580 --> 00:22.590
I like you.

00:25.090 --> 00:27.260
I'll keep you company for five minutes only.

00:30.510 --> 00:33.470
Optical camouflage!

00:40.270 --> 00:42.400
His thermal signature vanished too?

00:42.980 --> 00:44.400
No way...

00:44.400 --> 00:45.900
That's impossible!

00:57.080 --> 00:59.040
Clarin...

02:35.760 --> 02:37.510
"Don't get involved"?

02:39.100 --> 02:40.140
Clarin?

02:48.980 --> 02:50.940
Where did she go?

02:51.570 --> 02:55.410
Clarin, let's go shopping together!

03:02.540 --> 03:04.250
Hello! Clari—

03:02.910 --> 03:06.000
You have reached a voice mailbox.

03:06.000 --> 03:09.250
The person whom you are trying to call cannot be reached.

03:09.250 --> 03:13.420
Leave your message after the beep.

03:15.880 --> 03:17.890
Good morning, Takumi.

03:17.890 --> 03:19.510
Good morning, Nene!

03:19.510 --> 03:20.970
You're up early.

03:20.970 --> 03:23.430
So, I can't find Clarin.

03:23.850 --> 03:25.440
Do you know where she is?

03:25.440 --> 03:29.610
Oh, sure, I sent her on an errand for me.

03:30.110 --> 03:34.820
It has to do with company secrets, so you won't be able to contact her until she returns,

03:34.820 --> 03:36.070
but no need to worry.

03:36.070 --> 03:38.780
Oh, so that's why.

03:41.160 --> 03:42.540
What's the matter?

03:42.540 --> 03:47.330
I think... I might have made Clarin angry.

03:47.330 --> 03:49.080
What makes you think so?

03:50.040 --> 03:51.960
She left behind a note.

03:54.630 --> 03:57.550
I'm afraid I wouldn't know.

03:57.550 --> 03:58.800
All right.

03:59.640 --> 04:03.470
Sorry, but I need to focus on my work.

04:03.470 --> 04:05.730
It would help if you let me work.

04:05.730 --> 04:08.350
I'm sorry I bothered you!

04:12.730 --> 04:14.230
An errand...

04:14.650 --> 04:16.740
"Don't get involved."

04:17.400 --> 04:19.990
Does that mean Clarin wants me to stay away from her?

04:20.700 --> 04:22.990
Maybe it's because of before...

04:34.250 --> 04:35.510
Clarin!

04:38.930 --> 04:40.510
Nene, how are you!?

04:40.800 --> 04:43.050
H-Hi, I'm good.

04:43.050 --> 04:44.010
Guess what! Guess what!

04:44.010 --> 04:47.770
They're finally finished with our "temporary housing"!

04:47.770 --> 04:50.270
So let's play! Come over!

04:50.940 --> 04:52.020
Right now?

04:52.020 --> 04:54.110
Yeah! Let's play Monster Bash!

04:54.110 --> 04:55.480
Grandma's here too!

04:55.480 --> 04:57.150
Howdy, Nene!

04:57.150 --> 04:58.030
Howdy...

04:58.030 --> 05:00.280
You can come too, Clarin!

05:00.950 --> 05:02.030
Um...

05:02.950 --> 05:05.580
Clarin had to go somewhere today.

05:05.580 --> 05:08.750
Really? It's rare seeing you two apart.

05:08.750 --> 05:09.540
Yeah.

05:09.830 --> 05:11.120
But I get it.

05:11.120 --> 05:15.840
I love Grandma and all, but being around her <i>all</i> the time would get annoying.

05:16.550 --> 05:18.550
Amy, that hurts.

05:20.380 --> 05:21.430
Just kidding.

05:21.430 --> 05:23.180
Love you, Grandma!

05:23.890 --> 05:26.180
So hurry over, Nene!

05:26.180 --> 05:27.180
It's a promise!

05:27.180 --> 05:28.890
S-Sure.

05:38.360 --> 05:40.110
You're going to come with me?

05:41.650 --> 05:44.700
Being around her <i>all</i> the time would suck.

05:56.670 --> 05:59.510
Thank you. I'm fine, really.

06:00.420 --> 06:03.430
<i>I haven't fallen like that in a long time.</i>

06:04.930 --> 06:06.390
Hold yourself together, Nene.

06:13.690 --> 06:17.980
Because of Uzal's puppet I've come to understand a lot of things.

06:18.520 --> 06:20.860
I do feel bad for Nene, but...

06:26.780 --> 06:27.990
Good morning, everyone!

06:27.990 --> 06:29.620
Good morning, sir!

06:31.950 --> 06:36.750
Code Five, an American Imperial soldier started a brawl at Cenancle Hospital.

06:37.500 --> 06:38.790
Come on...

06:38.790 --> 06:41.050
How many times is that this month, now?

06:41.050 --> 06:43.260
Report it to the military police.

06:43.260 --> 06:46.510
It's out of our jurisdiction to arrest him, so there's nothing we can do to help.

06:56.770 --> 06:59.400
My name is Uzal Delilah.

06:59.400 --> 07:05.070
I'm a beauty, a genius, a scientist both wise and brilliant, and a legend short-lived.

07:06.200 --> 07:10.490
This information is, and was, to be sent to someone meeting certain requirements

07:10.490 --> 07:14.370
when Cenancle Island is confirmed to be in danger.

07:14.370 --> 07:15.290
Danger?

07:18.130 --> 07:19.290
That's...

07:19.290 --> 07:23.840
I entrust this information—these facts—to you.

07:23.840 --> 07:25.510
This is a warning.

07:35.230 --> 07:39.980
I've got an attorney on the line asking about the case where the American Imperial soldier injured a nurse.

07:41.820 --> 07:44.860
We're gonna end up taking the fall for that, aren't we?

07:44.860 --> 07:46.150
I'm stepping out for a bit.

07:46.150 --> 07:47.490
Cover for me.

07:51.450 --> 07:54.200
Something's eating at him.

07:54.200 --> 07:55.330
I'd say so.

07:55.330 --> 07:57.330
That laugh was shorter than usual.

07:57.920 --> 08:01.130
If he would just tell us, we'd help.

08:05.590 --> 08:06.970
Darn it!

08:07.930 --> 08:10.970
You're no fun today!

08:10.970 --> 08:12.220
S-Sorry!

08:12.560 --> 08:14.220
Are you bored of Monster Bash?

08:14.220 --> 08:16.100
No!

08:16.100 --> 08:19.730
We've played cards <i>and</i> Monster Bash,
but you're all spaced out!

08:20.770 --> 08:22.110
Are you even listening!?

08:22.820 --> 08:23.520
Clarin?

08:23.520 --> 08:25.610
I'm not Clarin!

08:25.610 --> 08:28.530
You're such a mess without her around.

08:28.530 --> 08:30.780
Th-That's not true.

08:30.780 --> 08:32.200
Yes it is!

08:32.200 --> 08:33.700
Is it?

08:33.700 --> 08:35.700
Boss!

08:35.700 --> 08:38.040
Boss, we've got a problem!

08:38.040 --> 08:38.830
David?

08:38.830 --> 08:39.580
Hurry!

08:39.870 --> 08:41.460
Lean's in trouble!

08:49.090 --> 08:51.890
You can climb trees, right, Boss?

08:51.890 --> 08:53.430
Y-Yeah...

08:53.430 --> 08:54.430
But...

08:55.350 --> 08:56.680
Nene!?

08:57.140 --> 08:58.640
<i>It's okay.</i>

08:58.640 --> 09:00.940
<i>I can handle this much alone!</i>

09:01.350 --> 09:03.150
Even without Clarin!

09:04.110 --> 09:06.230
Come on, let's get down.

09:07.280 --> 09:08.690
There's nothing to fear.

09:13.620 --> 09:14.620
Don't get involved.

09:16.370 --> 09:18.000
Nene!

09:26.250 --> 09:27.920
My instincts don't betray me!

09:27.920 --> 09:29.340
Robert!?

09:29.340 --> 09:31.680
Are you all right, Nene?

09:46.520 --> 09:47.900
Wait up!

09:48.690 --> 09:50.070
I'm sorry about that.

09:50.440 --> 09:52.820
I just don't have it together today.

09:52.820 --> 09:55.410
Nene, you seem down.

09:55.410 --> 09:56.830
Did something happen?

09:56.830 --> 09:59.250
No... Nothing...

10:00.160 --> 10:04.210
I should be able to do something by myself, I thought.

10:04.880 --> 10:07.710
Otherwise, Clarin will end up not liking me.

10:08.250 --> 10:11.220
Did you do something to make her dislike you?

10:11.220 --> 10:12.220
No!

10:12.590 --> 10:13.550
But...

10:16.220 --> 10:17.640
"Don't get involved."

10:18.220 --> 10:20.890
Don't get involved in what, though?

10:20.890 --> 10:22.600
I don't know.

10:22.600 --> 10:23.560
But...

10:24.100 --> 10:29.230
I thought it might mean she doesn't want me involved with her.

10:29.230 --> 10:30.900
What makes you think that?

10:30.900 --> 10:32.190
Well...

10:34.150 --> 10:37.160
Because I can't do anything on my own.

10:37.660 --> 10:42.290
Is Clarin the kind of girl who would dislike you for not being able to do anything?

10:42.290 --> 10:43.910
Not at all!

10:45.330 --> 10:49.840
It's just... I'm always relying on everyone else.

10:51.670 --> 10:53.720
I have ever since that day.

10:55.260 --> 10:59.430
And now, I'm always getting Clarin to help me.

11:00.470 --> 11:03.060
I need to be able to get things done myself.

11:05.310 --> 11:09.520
So you think reaching that goal will make
Clarin want to involve herself with you again?

11:10.440 --> 11:13.490
What do you think it means to be involved with someone?

11:13.490 --> 11:15.820
W-Well...

11:16.450 --> 11:19.070
It means to trust that person.

11:19.070 --> 11:20.580
Trust?

11:20.580 --> 11:24.370
How would you feel if Clarin was facing danger?

11:24.370 --> 11:25.330
I'd be worried!

11:25.710 --> 11:28.750
But what if you were told not to worry?

11:28.750 --> 11:29.750
Would you abandon her?

11:29.750 --> 11:31.460
I couldn't do such a thing!

11:31.920 --> 11:34.130
Even though you were told not to get involved?

11:34.720 --> 11:36.050
Yes, sir!

11:36.050 --> 11:37.930
I would still help Clarin!

11:37.930 --> 11:38.890
Why's that?

11:38.890 --> 11:40.140
Why would you help her?

11:41.350 --> 11:42.890
Because I want to.

11:42.890 --> 11:43.850
No!

11:44.350 --> 11:45.680
Because I love her!

11:47.190 --> 11:48.560
That's how we all are.

11:48.560 --> 11:53.530
It's important to remember that the people around you worry about you too.

11:53.530 --> 11:58.860
Peace doesn't need a single savior doing all the work for someone else.

11:59.990 --> 12:02.790
I believe help must be mutual to bring peace.

12:04.410 --> 12:07.080
You just need to try your hardest to do what you're capable of.

12:07.670 --> 12:12.500
What you can do that's within reach, for those important to you.

12:12.960 --> 12:15.010
Within reach...

12:16.380 --> 12:17.970
U-Um...

12:17.970 --> 12:20.840
I promised Clarin!

12:20.840 --> 12:23.140
I promised that we'd go shopping together!

12:23.510 --> 12:28.640
If you trust her, maybe all you need to do is wait for her.

12:29.060 --> 12:29.980
All right!

12:32.400 --> 12:35.280
Nene, be sure to come play again.

12:35.280 --> 12:37.190
Bring Clarin next time.

12:37.190 --> 12:37.900
Okay!

12:38.400 --> 12:40.950
Thank you, Robert.

12:40.950 --> 12:42.910
Ah, heck, I can't help it.

12:45.240 --> 12:48.910
Besides, maybe I'm the one who should be thanking you.

12:56.510 --> 12:58.670
An urgent matter?

12:59.470 --> 13:02.430
Just what is it, Captain Altman?

13:02.430 --> 13:04.680
I need to discuss something
extremely important with you.

13:05.100 --> 13:06.680
Chairman North, sir.

13:08.730 --> 13:09.730
What?

13:12.940 --> 13:15.230
Drugged and captured by a mysterious robot army,

13:15.230 --> 13:17.990
I managed to miraculously made my escape!

13:17.990 --> 13:20.240
Witness my journalistic spirit as I prowl around

13:20.240 --> 13:24.870
this menacing subterranean empire to bring these facts to the public!

13:24.870 --> 13:26.950
Hello. Hello!

13:28.790 --> 13:32.460
Bartender, hit us up with some fish dumpling and tofu fritters.

13:32.460 --> 13:33.710
You got it.

13:33.710 --> 13:36.340
Oh no, it's from you-know-who again.

13:36.340 --> 13:37.380
Hello, hello.

13:37.380 --> 13:43.090
Hel—me. I'm und—coverage—scoop—

13:44.640 --> 13:45.850
What was that about?

13:45.850 --> 13:46.890
Who knows?

13:46.890 --> 13:47.810
Huh?

13:48.220 --> 13:49.350
That's...

13:52.020 --> 13:53.060
Just you watch.

13:53.560 --> 13:56.400
I'll get this scoop if it kills me!

13:56.400 --> 14:00.990
I'm the intelligent super-dreadnought idol, Vli—

14:10.200 --> 14:11.460
Okay!

14:12.960 --> 14:15.210
An emergency summons by Captain Altman?

14:15.210 --> 14:16.960
Including our off-duty members?

14:16.960 --> 14:18.590
What on earth is...

14:22.970 --> 14:23.970
Officers!

14:26.220 --> 14:29.310
We are conducting a search of the AIA's facilities!

14:30.430 --> 14:32.600
I'll explain the details in due course,

14:32.600 --> 14:36.190
but the peace of Cenacle Island depends on this search!

14:36.360 --> 14:37.230
Captain...

14:37.560 --> 14:41.570
We have a legal basis worked out, but politically, it's going to be an adventure.

14:42.110 --> 14:43.650
That's why I won't order you.

14:48.120 --> 14:50.870
I'm making this a request!

14:50.870 --> 14:54.620
I want you to help me, for the sake of this island's peace.

14:58.000 --> 15:00.000
Sir, yes, sir!

15:00.000 --> 15:02.630
We were waiting to hear those words!

15:02.630 --> 15:03.670
We are prepared to go!

15:03.670 --> 15:05.510
Let's teach them a lesson!

15:10.260 --> 15:12.020
I told you, it's not an order!

15:12.560 --> 15:15.390
But I guess you guys are ready, then!?

15:15.390 --> 15:17.230
Sir, yes, sir!

15:22.030 --> 15:27.070
I'll have this place ready for Clarin to come home!

15:29.530 --> 15:30.950
I've returned, Nene.

15:30.950 --> 15:32.540
Welcome home, Clarin!

15:32.540 --> 15:34.200
You must be tired after your errand.

15:34.200 --> 15:35.580
Would you like to charge?

15:35.580 --> 15:37.040
Or do you need maintenance?

15:37.420 --> 15:38.540
Such beauty in here.

15:40.040 --> 15:42.840
I worked hard to clean the place up for you!

15:42.840 --> 15:43.670
No.

15:43.670 --> 15:44.300
Huh?

15:46.010 --> 15:47.680
<i>You're</i> the beauty.

15:48.140 --> 15:49.680
So beautiful, I hardly recognized you.

15:49.680 --> 15:51.810
C-Clarin!

15:51.810 --> 15:55.230
You can even paw my ears, Nene.

15:55.230 --> 15:56.940
Y-You sure?

15:59.230 --> 16:04.690
Clarin, your ears feel nice and fluffy.

16:04.690 --> 16:09.530
Yes, scratchy, fluffy, scratchy...

16:09.530 --> 16:10.700
Scratchy?

16:14.790 --> 16:15.580
Thou art late!

16:15.580 --> 16:17.580
Late, dark, cramped!

16:17.580 --> 16:20.290
I loathe the darkness!

16:20.290 --> 16:22.420
Sorry, I completely forgot.

16:23.340 --> 16:25.670
A cruel angel's thesis!

16:25.670 --> 16:29.050
We have not maidens enough to heal this damage!

16:29.050 --> 16:31.390
Not enough! 'Twill not rise! I cannot persist!

16:31.390 --> 16:33.930
To quote Goethe, "More maidens!"

16:33.930 --> 16:36.060
Clarin is out running an errand.

16:36.480 --> 16:38.560
Aye, that I know.

16:38.560 --> 16:44.440
By all accounts, she hath snuck into the geofront in order to stop my body from rampaging.

16:45.070 --> 16:45.820
Huh?

17:14.810 --> 17:17.060
Puppet! Dodge that!

17:20.480 --> 17:22.600
That's not optical camouflage.

17:22.600 --> 17:25.020
It's thermo-optical camouflage!

17:25.020 --> 17:29.820
Not even my companies or the long-established Kyo-Re have developed that kind of tech yet...

17:29.820 --> 17:30.820
Don't tell me...

17:35.830 --> 17:38.120
Watch out for his claws!

17:38.120 --> 17:41.620
Your opponent has military-grade cyborg arms!

17:42.750 --> 17:45.630
They easily destroyed Shinokaomi's armor!

17:46.130 --> 17:49.420
Don't even think about trying to block them head-on!

18:06.690 --> 18:08.150
Not a bad performance.

18:08.690 --> 18:12.950
Not long ago, I would have yearned to obtain this specimen unscathed even at the cost of time,

18:12.950 --> 18:15.570
but the plan is too far along its final stage.

18:16.160 --> 18:18.580
Wasting time is a hobby of fools.

18:18.910 --> 18:20.200
It matters not.

18:20.200 --> 18:21.410
Destroy it.

18:27.840 --> 18:28.920
So fast!

18:28.920 --> 18:33.510
With that mobility, just how mechanized <i>is</i> this guy!?

18:39.220 --> 18:40.810
We're in trouble!

18:55.820 --> 18:57.070
Puppet!

18:56.320 --> 18:57.070
What?

19:14.840 --> 19:16.800
<i>What the hell is happening!?</i>

19:16.800 --> 19:19.140
<i>This is no time to be unconscious!</i>

19:19.140 --> 19:23.980
<i>If I'm of no use to the colonel,
he really will do away with us all!</i>

19:44.910 --> 19:45.910
Puppet!

19:45.910 --> 19:47.670
That's no cyborg!

19:47.670 --> 19:49.210
It's an android!

20:06.980 --> 20:08.730
It transformed!?

20:08.730 --> 20:09.480
This means...

20:15.610 --> 20:17.860
No, we're not losing ground!

20:17.860 --> 20:18.860
This'll work!

20:18.860 --> 20:20.660
Ta-dah!

20:20.660 --> 20:23.160
Reinforcements have arrived, Colonel Kurtz!

20:24.870 --> 20:26.910
So we're beating her up, eh?

20:26.910 --> 20:28.080
I'll help out!

20:28.080 --> 20:30.540
I may not look it, but I can handle weapons—

20:31.460 --> 20:32.380
Huh?

20:35.880 --> 20:37.420
<i>Don't kill anybody!</i>

20:59.950 --> 21:01.240
Five minutes.

21:07.500 --> 21:10.120
I won't let the puppet's death be in vain.

21:12.790 --> 21:14.590
I'm going to go find Clarin!

21:14.590 --> 21:17.880
Clarin, I <i>will</i> involve myself with you!

21:17.880 --> 21:19.260
I shall go too!

21:19.260 --> 21:21.300
Okay, I'll go let Takumi know.

21:21.300 --> 21:23.890
Wait, o too innocent maiden.

21:25.760 --> 21:30.600
The maiden who harboreth that limitless plain upon herself is most busy at present.

21:30.600 --> 21:31.900
Oh, she is?

21:31.900 --> 21:34.360
Therefore, simply leave a message.

21:36.150 --> 21:38.610
So um, I hold you like this?

21:38.610 --> 21:39.360
Indeed...

21:39.820 --> 21:42.410
With thy fingers gently wrapped around me.

21:42.410 --> 21:44.620
But be careful with those nails.

21:44.950 --> 21:48.700
Then thrust my leg into the room's terminal.

21:51.540 --> 21:53.380
Wow!

21:53.380 --> 21:57.380
Nene, thou hast magic hands!

22:00.920 --> 22:02.050
We may go...

22:04.010 --> 22:04.890
Nene is...

22:05.640 --> 22:07.390
studying.

22:08.060 --> 22:11.020
Now if I can just seize control of BUER...

22:13.020 --> 22:15.310
Our escape is a success.

22:16.400 --> 22:18.730
Here I come, Clarin!

22:41.050 --> 22:44.050
Accessing the device named nature

22:44.050 --> 22:47.050
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:47.050 --> 22:47.600
read

22:47.600 --> 22:48.140
write

22:48.140 --> 22:48.810
enter

22:48.810 --> 22:49.430
code

22:49.430 --> 22:52.810
Sharing tools can lead to unavoidable situations

22:53.520 --> 23:04.110
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:54.060 --> 22:55.480
Lovely bride of mine,

22:55.480 --> 22:57.980
I want you to touch my ears with your beautiful fingers.

22:57.980 --> 22:58.690
C-Clarin!

22:58.690 --> 23:00.780
Nene, I could be yours for all of time.

23:00.780 --> 23:02.030
Cat prince Clarin!

23:02.030 --> 23:03.610
Stay with me forever!

23:04.110 --> 23:05.490
Saving data

23:05.490 --> 23:06.870
Strengthening predictions

23:06.870 --> 23:09.870
Even my latest updates

23:09.870 --> 23:15.170
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.170 --> 23:16.750
Error error

23:16.750 --> 23:18.250
parameter

23:18.250 --> 23:21.630
Please help me understand

23:21.630 --> 23:23.800
where these emotions came from.

23:23.800 --> 23:26.970
Find me at the end of this labrynth

23:26.970 --> 23:29.720
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.720 --> 23:31.720
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.720 --> 23:35.100
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.480 --> 23:38.100
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.440 --> 23:40.860
and head straight to you

23:40.860 --> 23:43.280
I won't come to understand love

23:43.280 --> 23:47.030
without having you here with me

23:52.490 --> 23:53.790
Here I come, Clarin!

23:53.790 --> 23:54.910
I'm on my way!

23:54.910 --> 23:58.000
Spirits that call to one another, maiden attracted to maiden.

23:58.000 --> 24:00.500
Ah, 'tis water for my parched heart!

24:00.500 --> 24:03.250
Well, after all, I love Clarin!

24:03.250 --> 24:05.550
'Tis for this cupful I do live!
